  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Point P and Q are located on different equipotential surfaces in a gravitational field. The values shown are in MJ kg<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>. A small object with mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"200\"></span> g moves from point P to point Q.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>What is the magnitude of the work done by the gravitational field on the object?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1\"></span> kJ</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4\"></span> kJ</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10\"></span> kJ</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40\"></span> kJ</li>\n</ol>"
  },
